      "link": "https://t.me/zaihua_news/2999",
      "published": "2026-10-20T14:31:53+00:00",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Nvidia recently rejected several emerging cloud service providers from attending the upcoming GTC conference in Berlin. The reason for rejection was not that they failed to meet technical standards, but that these providers had introduced rival chips such as AMD GPUs and Google TPUs into their own cloud platforms. Nvidia has not yet publicly commented on the incident. Nvidia is a chip supplier and also a major investor in emerging cloud providers such as CoreWeave and Nebius; it has made a strategic investment of $2 billion in each and also provided revenue backstops for their compute leasing. Many emerging cloud providers with limited scale do not dare to publicly use Nvidia's rival products, fearing that their priority GPU supply, financing, and IPO plans will be affected. This restriction does not apply to hyperscale cloud providers with sufficient purchasing volume and in-house chip capabilities.",
        "快科技"
      ],
